@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# Local arm64 build
+
+The baseline is official Squirrel 1.1.2, commit `876adebaf2f612951dcdca8a591de65401222b9a`. Upstream GPL license is retained in `LICENSE.txt`. The `Sparkle` and `librime` submodules are pinned by upstream; their own licenses remain in their source directories.
+
+This builds the macOS frontend from source while reusing the matching official Squirrel 1.1.2 runtime libraries and bundled dictionaries. It does not rebuild librime or Sparkle. `LOCAL-DEPENDENCIES.json` records their provenance and binary checksums.
+
+Requirements: Apple Silicon, Xcode 26.2, Python 3, official Squirrel 1.1.2 installed in the user input-method directory (or pass `--official-app PATH`).
+
+```sh
+git submodule update --init --depth 1 Sparkle librime
+python3 scripts/build-local.py --configuration Release
+```
+
+The app is written to `build/Build/Products/Release/Squirrel.app`, ad-hoc signed, and checked with `codesign --verify --deep --strict`. Its `--help` command is run as a dynamic-link smoke test; this returns before creation of the input server. The script never copies into an input-method directory, explicitly registers a TIS input source, unregisters an app, or normally launches the app.
+
+Xcode 26.2 automatically registers its generated app with LaunchServices and ignores `REGISTER_WITH_LAUNCH_SERVICES=NO`. **Do not run `lsregister -u` on a build with the same bundle ID as the installed input method**: it can invalidate the installed app's mapping too. The build script leaves this automatic Xcode state alone. After placing the final app at its installed path, the installer must invoke that installed app's `--register-input-source` command before starting it.
+
+The custom registration command uses `Bundle.main.bundleURL`, forces `LSRegisterURL`, calls `TISRegisterInputSource`, and refreshes registration even if a Squirrel mode is already enabled. It preserves a nonempty enabled-mode set and the current input-source selection. An empty pre-registration snapshot can occur while replacing the bundle; that recovery/fresh-install state restores the default Hans mode instead of disabling newly registered sources. The command reports `expectedEnabledModes` plus actual API statuses as JSON and returns a meaningful process exit code. Bounded polling pumps the run loop to receive asynchronous TIS state changes. `tools/manage_frontend.py` independently validates the expected-mode policy and actual installed process path. Legacy rollback uses the same recovery policy through explicit actual-path LS/TIS calls because official Squirrel 1.1.2 has a broken hardcoded registration path.
+
+When running under a restricted filesystem sandbox, Xcode's resource compiler may require access to the normal macOS build services. A resource-compiler failure does not imply a Swift source error; inspect `build-local-release.log`.
+
+Layout demonstrations should run as a separate panel-only harness without `Main.swift` and without starting `IMKServer`. Do not launch the built app as an input method until the parent task has completed its testing and deployment preparation.
